I can't make this edit yet, because I can't see `app/src/tides.ts`. Every SEARCH block has to match the file's text exactly once, and I'd only be guessing at the body of `closeFor`. A wrong guess would be refused, or worse, would match something unintended.

Please paste the contents of `app/src/tides.ts`, or at least `closeFor` and the types it uses (the window type and the return value). With that I'll send a single edit that:

- adds a constant for the 12-minute locking time;
- keeps a leftover piece on either side of a cut window only if it is at least 12 minutes long (exactly 12 stays);
- adds the minutes of any dropped piece to the returned count;
- leaves windows the closure doesn't touch as they are, however short.

One thing I'll check once I see the code is the unit of the window times (minutes or timestamps). The 12-minute threshold and the lost-minutes count have to use the same unit.
